{"aggregate_id": "01M4RKRDC5ZBJM399WMDFC20K9", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M4RKRJC32RFQB8QPHHR4FF21", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn.dejongh@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-10-12T17:49:52.028139+00:00", "friendly_name": "Derive the mission-state audit's CI trigger list from what the audit executes", "mission_id": "01M4RKRDC5ZBJM399WMDFC20K9", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "audit-trigger-derivation-01M4RKRD", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "The mission-state audit's CI trigger (ci-router.yml mission_state group) and a second copy in tests (AUDIT_INPUT_PATHS) are both hand-written from a one-time call trace, so they can drift from the modules the audit actually executes and from each other. When the audit executes a module outside the globs, a PR that changes the audit's verdict skips the audit (the #6058 incident), caught only by the nightly backstop after merge. This mission adds a non-vacuous test that derives the executed-module set from an in-process audit run and removes the hand copy.", "purpose_tldr": "Replace the two hand-copied lists of the modules the mission-state audit touches with one derived, drift-proof check.", "target_branch": "issue-6090-audit-trigger-derivation", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-12T17:49:56.995699+00:00"}
